1
00:00:00,414 --> 00:00:02,044
(Sheldon:)- He's a famous physicist...
- Yeah.

2
00:00:02,207 --> 00:00:05,707
l know. He's the wheelchair dude
who invented time.

3
00:00:08,839 --> 00:00:10,719
(Sheldon:)Close enough.

4
00:00:10,883 --> 00:00:13,763
(Penny:)Why doesn't Howard
just introduce you to the guy?

5
00:00:13,927 --> 00:00:17,927
(Sheldon:)Because he's punishing me
for being a, quote, "condescending jerk."

6
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:20,560
(Sheldon:)You don't think I'm condescending,
do you?

7
00:00:21,226 --> 00:00:23,516
- Well...
- Oh, I'm sorry.

8
00:00:23,687 --> 00:00:25,937
(Sheldon:)- Condescending means...
- l know what it means!

9
00:00:26,899 --> 00:00:29,739
(Penny:)And, yes, you love correcting people
and putting them down.

10
00:00:29,902 --> 00:00:34,072
(Sheldon:)Au contraire, when I correct people,
l am raising them up.

11
00:00:36,408 --> 00:00:38,748
(Sheldon:)You should know.
l do it for you more than anyone.

12
00:00:41,038 --> 00:00:43,078
(Penny:)Come on, you do it to feel superior.

13
00:00:43,248 --> 00:00:46,458
l see that twinkle when someone
says "who" instead of "whom"...

14
00:00:46,669 --> 00:00:49,759
(Penny:)...or thinks the moon is a planet.

15
00:00:49,922 --> 00:00:53,672
(Sheldon:)Or Don Quixote is a book
about a donkey named Hotay.

16
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:57,430
See? There it is. There's that twinkle.

17
00:00:57,596 --> 00:01:01,026
(Sheldon:)Well, I can't help it.
That's an involuntary twinkle.

